   "Japan\u2019s debt-to-GDP ratio of 230% is misleading because it ignores the asset side of the public sector balance sheet, which has evolved into a massive, leveraged investment portfolio.",
   "The Japanese public sector effectively operates a national-scale carry trade: borrowing at low rates via BOJ bank reserves and investing in domestic equities and unhedged foreign securities.",
   "This strategy has been highly successful, with net consolidated liabilities falling from 117% of GDP in 2012 to approximately 65% in 2025.",
